{"summary": "I wrote history.md (Russian summary on top, details in English). It collects what Maxim and the agents said and decided about inventory, tool craft and building, from 27.10 to 04.11. Each item has its source and file:line, and each topic is in a table of decision, status in code and open question. I read the code but ran no Godot or browser, so "exists" rests on reading plus the task notes (bots green at the time).

Building by volume exists. There are 12 fixed pieces on a 1 m grid (8 wood, 4 stone), costed in m³ only. Wood comes from lying logs and loose timber within 20 m, stone from loose stones, and everything built can be broken (PieceBreaker). The wood and stone balances stay exact to about 1e-15 m³ in the bots.

These are not in the code at all:
- a free-form editor with gizmos or combine;
- .obj/.glb import (grep finds none);
- the exact volume of an arbitrary mesh;
- the craft of a tool from two materials (F6);
- the matter ledger (F7);
- shape wear (F5).

Building ignores the bag. `_wood_plan` (build_system.gd:501-548) counts only world logs and loose timber, so wood in the inventory cannot be spent on a wall.

The inventory is built. It has 36 cells, two hands, a belt, a Tab/I inventory with drag and drop, items under 10 kg going into the bag, and a 3D detail panel with hard/loose ticks. Not built: the bag volume limit from GDD-v4 (40 L / 25 kg), the stones-of-expertise UI, and world buttons.

GDD-v4 is stale. §11 (docs/GDD-v4.md:232-235) still forbids the craft menu, free forging of shape and destruction of buildings, and Maxim asked for all three.

Verbatim Russian quotes are stored only for 01.11 (backlog), 02.11 and 04.11, plus a few words. Messages from 27.10-31.10 exist in the repo only as English translations inside workflow briefs. I marked those as translated and invented no Russian.

Concept images: H_freeform_build_3d_v1.png exists, but nothing records whether Maxim approved it. G_inventory_craft_v1.png was never generated because the generator blocked it twice for "violence".

